  "verbalization": "Oleiferin C is shown to have targets that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through multiple pathways. The first pathway links Oleiferin C to D-263MG, which is targeted by 6-Bromo-1H-Indole-4,7-Diol, a compound that directly interacts with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second and third pathways indicate that Oleiferin C also targets Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is further targeted by two different compounds, both of which also interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Oleiferin C may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through different molecular mechanisms, potentially by modulating the expression or activity of its targets. The evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, indicating a possible role for Oleiferin C in regulating the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
